{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>But the sons of Korah did not die.</b> Scripture informed of this matter here and not at the place of the main event, nor did it write it in the place of the counting of the Levites, for there is the place to inform of the dead among them — according to what we have written, that here Elohim came to fix the sin upon Dathan and Abiram and to lighten it from upon Korah. Therefore it concluded by saying <b>but the sons of Korah did not die</b> — the intention being that this proclaims the merit of their father, that his sin did not sweep them away in the manner that it swept away the sin of Dathan and Abiram, all their households, they being the principals of the dispute."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:38.569932811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}